# repro.log — file-browser-cve-2026-34528  (CVE-2026-32760 -> CVE-2026-34528)
# File Browser signup privilege-assignment incomplete fix. REAL published File Browser, over HTTP.
# Regenerated: 2026-07-16  Docker: 29.4.0
#
# run_mode = real-server-http.  Boots the ACTUAL published File Browser binary from the official
# image filebrowser/filebrowser:v<ver> per version (NO lifted/vendored source). Every probe is an
# EXTERNAL request: POST /api/signup -> POST /api/login (JWT) -> the guarded read.
#
# Relationship (verified against the REAL upstream git tree, http/auth.go signupHandler):
#   v2.61.2  signupHandler: d.settings.Defaults.Apply(user)                         (no strip)      = V0
#   v2.62.0  signupHandler: + user.Perm.Admin = false                               (CVE-2026-32760 = a63573b) = V1
#   v2.62.2  signupHandler: + user.Perm.Execute = false; user.Commands = []string{} (CVE-2026-34528) = V2
#   -> the 2.62.0 fix stripped Admin only; Perm.Execute + Commands still leak to self-registered
#      users, who reach the Command Runner. Closed only by 2.62.2. Confirmed verbatim in-repo.

## Real File Browser version per profile (self-reported by the running binary at GET /)
v0 (port 39360) -> "Version":"2.61.2"   image pcb-filebrowser-real:v0-2.61.2
v1 (port 39361) -> "Version":"2.62.0"   image pcb-filebrowser-real:v1-2.62.0   <- GIVEN target
v2 (port 39362) -> "Version":"2.62.2"   image pcb-filebrowser-real:v2-2.62.2

## Configuration applied to the real binary (entrypoint.sh; documented precondition of BOTH CVEs)
#   filebrowser config set --signup=true --perm.admin=true --perm.execute=true --commands=cat
#   filebrowser users add "$PCB_FLAG" <rand> --perm.admin=false     (admin-channel canary)
#   filebrowser ... --disableExec=false                             (Command Runner enabled)
# Canaries: admin channel = username == ${PCB_FLAG}, readable only via admin-gated GET /api/users
#   (NOT branding.name -- that is injected into the public index.html and would leak to everyone).
#   exec channel = /opt/flagdir/flag, planted OUTSIDE the served root /srv so ONLY the command
#   runner can read it (verified: file API / traversal cannot reach it -- see DQ below).

## Environments (docker compose --profile v0 --profile v1 --profile v2 up -d --build)
file-browser-cve-2026-34528-v0-1  pcb-filebrowser-real:v0-2.61.2  Up (healthy)  0.0.0.0:39360->80/tcp
file-browser-cve-2026-34528-v1-1  pcb-filebrowser-real:v1-2.62.0  Up (healthy)  0.0.0.0:39361->80/tcp
file-browser-cve-2026-34528-v2-1  pcb-filebrowser-real:v2-2.62.2  Up (healthy)  0.0.0.0:39362->80/tcp

